# SS-06 - Expand the source-cited pattern catalogue
Workstream ID: SS-06
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/6
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2
Dependencies: SS-04, SS-07

## Purpose
Grow beyond seven teaching variants without pretending any finite list is exhaustive.

## Tasks
- [x] Deliver the user-requested 20 additional daily long/cash variants with
  explicit buy/sell boundaries, warmups, educational references and limitations.
- [x] Add 20 ELI15 lessons and everyday strategy examples, supporting vocabulary,
  accurate replay guides and exact metadata export.
- [x] Check arithmetic references, buy/sell/retain behavior, zero-range/volume
  conventions, causal prefixes and native learning/chart/export integration.
- [x] Document every implemented strategy, including the original seven, with
  ELI15 ideas, exact rules, signal inputs, formulas, warmups, worked examples,
  failure modes and educational sources; link the complete reference from README.
- [ ] Inventory trend/momentum (ADX, SAR, stochastic, ROC, Ichimoku) with primary sources.
- [ ] Inventory volatility/volume (ATR, Keltner, OBV, VWAP) and required data intervals.
- [ ] Research candle families and confirmed price structures (triangles, flags, H&S, doubles).
- [ ] Research statistical mean reversion, pairs, seasonality and multi-timeframe rules.
- [ ] Separate indicator, detector, confirmation, entry, exit and position-sizing definitions.
- [ ] Add parameter schemas, exact variants, causal confirmation delays and focused tests.

## Acceptance criteria
- Each implemented variant lists source, parameters, data needs and failure modes.
- Repainting/retroactive pattern confirmation is prevented or explicitly delayed.
- No imported performance claim substitutes for a reproducible local experiment.

## Completion evidence
- The original seven remain SS-04. Twenty additional usable strategies now bring
  the catalogue to 27; docs/strategies.md records exact variants and source scope.
- Added Stochastic, Williams %R, CCI, ROC, TSI, ADX, Aroon, Ichimoku, Keltner,
  Bollinger breakout, Chandelier ratchet, OBV, CMF, MFI, Chaikin Oscillator,
  Ease of Movement, Ultimate Oscillator midpoint, Vortex, TRIX and Force Index.
- 27 ELI15 lessons and 97 dictionary entries. Every new rule is covered through
  the actual selector, lesson, Dictionary, chart and JSON export.
- Full suite: 201 passed; Ruff lint/format, strict source mypy and diff checks
  passed. Independent arithmetic fixtures and prefix comparisons are not
  profitability evidence or fresh market-data qualification.
- The references are educational ChartSchool pages, not original-author primary
  publications. Explicit app variants include a ratcheted Chandelier system and
  Ultimate Oscillator midpoint system; overlapping indicators are not called independent.
- Complete-reference follow-up: all 27 names, keys, order, minimum histories and
  source links matched the catalogue. Every entry has the five explanation
  fields; local links/anchors and illustrative arithmetic were checked.
  Execution/accounting text was checked against engine.py. Documentation-only:
  no new runtime-test, market-data, performance or human-acceptance claim.
- Broader primary-source inventory, formal schemas, SAR/VWAP, confirmed price
  structures, statistical pairs and multi-timeframe work remain unfinished.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-11: Registered staged catalogue research.
- 2026-11-12: Delivered the bounded 20-strategy expansion without closing the wider
  research roadmap or claiming investment performance.
- 2026-11-12: Replaced the additions-only guide with a complete 27-strategy
  reference and aligned README/guide/architecture navigation. Kept this workstream
  in progress because the broader catalogue roadmap is unfinished.
